  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-antigravity-auth",
      "text": "[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-antigravity-auth)\n[](https://awesome-dsh-plugin.com)\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nUse your Antigravity account in [DeepSeek Harness (DSH)](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) for language models, web search, image creation, and experimental video understanding. One shared login also powers the usage dashboard. Cache multiple accounts locally and switch between them manually, with **one active account at a time**."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-antigravity-auth",
      "text": "> **Unofficial, experimental, personal use only.** Google does not support third-party Antigravity login tools; your account may be suspended or terminated. Read the [Google FAQ](https://antigravity.google/docs/faq/) and [Additional Terms](https://antigravity.google/terms) before signing in. Private endpoints can change or stop working without notice. Do not rely on this plugin for production workloads."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-antigravity-auth",
      "text": "**Current release:** `0.1.5` (`latest`). See [Releases](https://github.com/suntianc/dsh-antigravity-auth/releases) and [CHANGELOG](CHANGELOG.md) for version history.\n\n[Quick start](#quick-start) · [Using the capabilities](#using-the-capabilities) · [Account commands](#account-commands) · [Troubleshooting](#troubleshooting) · [Development](#development)"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it provides",
      "text": "| Capability | DSH entry point |\n| --- | --- |\n| Language models | `google-antigravity` provider in the model selector, with Gemini, Claude, and GPT-OSS routes subject to account availability |\n| Web search | `antigravity` search provider for the stock `web_search` tool |\n| Image generation and editing | `generate_image`, plus `list_images` for saved session images |\n| Experimental video understanding | `analyze_video` for MP4 files in the active workspace |\n| Account and quota status | **Settings → Antigravity**, with five-hour and weekly quota windows and English/Chinese UI |"
    },
    {
      "section": "1. Check requirements",
      "text": "- A working DSH installation. The tested development baseline is **DSH `0.2.1-rc.5`**.\n- Node.js `^22.19.0` or `>=24.0.0`, and `pnpm` on `PATH` (`11.7.0` is the project's tested version).\n- A Google account with Antigravity access.\n- A local Host and browser for OAuth. Web account actions require the Host's WebServer to be explicitly bound to **`127.0.0.1`**; the temporary OAuth callback uses **`127.0.0.1:51121`**."
    },
    {
      "section": "1. Check requirements",
      "text": "The package does not restrict the DSH peer version range. That allows installation on other versions, but does **not** establish compatibility. See the [verification scope](docs/dsh-source-verification.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "2. Install or upgrade",
      "text": "Stop the Host using the target profile, then run:\n\n```sh\ndsh --version\ndsh plugin --profile web add --save-exact dsh-antigravity-auth@0.1.5\ndsh plugin --profile web list\n```\n\nReplace `web` with your actual profile, such as `desktop`. Confirm the listed version, restart that Host (for the Web profile, `dsh web`), and refresh the client."
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Sign in",
      "text": "1. Open **Settings → Antigravity** and choose **Start Antigravity login**. Starting login records acknowledgement of the unofficial-channel risk above.\n2. Complete Google authorization in the browser on the Host machine. If the new tab is blocked, use **Open the Google authorization page** in the settings card.\n3. Return to DSH and check the login result. Run `/anti status` for detailed capability status. If authorization expires, cancel it or start a new login.\n4. Select an available `google-antigravity` model. In the Antigravity settings cards, enable the Search, Image, or Video capabilities you want to use."
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Sign in",
      "text": "Login and a usable project are required. The normal Host automatically activates capability gates for the account; this is **not a live test of every model or tool**. Actual availability still depends on the account and private backend. A disabled control also needs a writable Host settings scope.\n\nFor terminal login, see [Account commands](#account-commands)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Using the capabilities",
      "text": "- **Models:** choose `google-antigravity` in DSH's model selector. The plugin also registers `google` as an alias when no other provider owns it. Live discovery filters the pinned model catalog; if discovery is temporarily unavailable, the selector may show an advisory snapshot rather than confirmed availability.\n- **Search:** select `antigravity` in the Host's **Web Search** provider configuration when multiple providers are installed. Enabling the Antigravity card alone does not replace DSH's selected provider. The stock `web_search` tool then returns grounded results with source links.\n- **Images:** ask DSH to generate an image, or edit an explicit session image (`image:<id>`) or workspace image. `generate_image` accepts a prompt, up to **5 references**, an optional model, and requests for **1–4 images** (`n`). Partial success can return fewer images with warnings. Images are saved as session attachments and can be found with `list_images`. Dedicated size, aspect-ratio, quality, and transparency parameters are not implemented.\n- **Video:** provide an explicit MP4 path inside the active workspace and a question for `analyze_video`. The default and maximum file limit is **32 MiB**"
    },
    {
      "section": "Account commands",
      "text": "On interactive DSH surfaces that support slash commands, `/anti` is an alias for `/antigravity-auth`:\n\n```text\n/anti status       # Show login and capability status (also the default action)\n/anti login        # Start Google OAuth and activate the signed-in account\n/anti cancel       # Cancel a pending login\n/anti accounts     # List locally cached accounts"
    },
    {
      "section": "Account commands",
      "text": "- Successful login caches the account in `accounts.json` and makes it active in `auth.json`. Other cached accounts remain until explicitly removed. There is no automatic rotation or quota pool.\n- Local logout removes only that account's local credential; it does not revoke the Google grant. Removing an active cached account can activate another remaining account, or log out when none remains.\n- Commands work on a local Host without a WebServer, or with one explicitly bound to `127.0.0.1`. They are blocked when the shared command interface is exposed on another address.\n- Terminal login opens the Host's browser and deliberately does not print the authorization URL into persisted session output. It cannot complete the interactive handoff on a headless Host without a usable browser. After browser authorization, run `/anti status`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Troubleshooting",
      "text": "| Symptom | What to check |\n| --- | --- |\n| Settings section missing, or `loopback-required` | Confirm the plugin is installed in the running profile, restart the Host, and refresh the client. Account RPC requires an explicit `127.0.0.1` WebServer bind; a loopback-looking client URL alone is not enough. Non-loopback connections hide the section. |\n| Login does not open a browser | In Settings, use **Open the Google authorization page**. If the link never appears, check the displayed error and confirm the installed version is `0.1.5` or newer. The terminal command has no printed-link fallback. |\n| Callback port in use, or authorization expired | Identify the process using `127.0.0.1:51121`; close it only if safe, then start a fresh login. Expired or cancelled authorization links cannot be reused. |\n| Logged in, but a capability is unavailable | Check project availability, the capability status, its enabled setting, and the Host settings scope. A successful login is not proof that the backend accepts every capability. |\n| Search still uses another provider | Set the Host's Web Search provider to `antigravity`; the plugin preserves the existing selection. |\n| `invalid_grant` / login r"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile\npnpm run check\n```\n\n`check` runs peer checks, lint, type checks, offline tests, Host/client builds, package smoke checks, and publint. Live OAuth and private endpoint checks are separate opt-in operations; an offline pass does not verify a real account.\n\nThe [bundle patch](cordis.patch.yml) installs four Host rows: `antigravity-auth` (shared authentication and LLM), `antigravity-search`, `antigravity-image`, and `antigravity-video`."
    },
